# Canonical identity for every commit in this repository.
#
# All five author strings below are the same person. Recorded here rather
# than rewritten into the commits because a history rewrite would change
# every SHA on a pushed main -- 689 commits as of 2026-08-02 -- invalidating
# every SHA cited in docs/AUDIT_REGISTER.md, CHANGELOG.md and the merged PRs.
#
# git log/shortlog/blame and GitHub all honour this file, so authorship
# reads as one identity everywhere it matters -- including for the
# sole-copyright basis of the commercial licence offer.
#
# Verify with:  git log --format='%aN <%aE>' | sort -u
# (one line out; %an/%ae ignore this file and will show all five)
#
# The COMMITTER of a rebase-merged commit is GitHub <noreply@github.com>,
# which this file does not map and should not: committer is who applied the
# patch, not who wrote it, and the copyright claim rests on authorship.
